From: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 22:25:00 +0000
Subject: irqchip/meson-gpio: allow GPIO interrupts to act as wakeup sources

meson_gpio_irq_chip provides neither .irq_set_wake nor
IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE, so enable_irq_wake() returns -ENXIO for every
interrupt behind it and the interrupt is masked on the way into suspend.

On ODROID-HC4 the PCF8563 alarm is such an interrupt, so the board enters
suspend-to-idle with nothing left to wake it: the alarm never fires and
only a power cycle brings the board back.

Claim IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE, the way 35 other drivers under
drivers/irqchip do.  The parent interrupt controller is the GIC, which
has no wakeup state of its own, so handing the request upwards with
irq_chip_set_wake_parent would fail instead.

Signed-off-by: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
---
 drivers/irqchip/irq-meson-gpio.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/irqchip/irq-meson-gpio.c b/drivers/irqchip/irq-meson-gpio.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-meson-gpio.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-meson-gpio.c
@@ -450,7 +450,7 @@ static struct irq_chip meson_gpio_irq_chip = {
 #ifdef CONFIG_SMP
 	.irq_set_affinity	= irq_chip_set_affinity_parent,
 #endif
-	.flags			= IRQCHIP_SET_TYPE_MASKED,
+	.flags			= IRQCHIP_SET_TYPE_MASKED | IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE,
 };
 
 static int meson_gpio_irq_domain_translate(struct irq_domain *domain,
